			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync submodules with worker bootstrap fix and dependency updates\n\nMulti-component synchronization bringing stability and dependency updates:\n\n1. **Output**: Add RewritePerfBaselineWorker transform to fix timer service worker bootstrap crashes. The transform removes `__name(...)` decoration from `(function() {...}).toString()` source that gets mangled by Vite when inlined into Astro chunks, causing `ReferenceError: Can't find variable: $4e` at runtime. Also fixes Tauri's `.env` overriding Build.sh's `NODE_ENV` by gating debug profiles on `Debug=true`.\n\n2. **Mountain**: Update build.rs comments to document PascalCase environment variable naming convention (`Profile`, `Pack`, `Bundle`, `Compiler`) introduced in the 2026-04-29 migration, replacing legacy `LAND_*` names.\n\n3. **Sky**: Bump Astro from 6.1.9 to 6.1.10 and remove unused empty `.env.example` template file.\n\n4. **Cocoon**: Sync to latest upstream extension host implementation.\n\nImpact: Timer service worker now boots correctly without mangled reference errors. Debug builds properly use readable output.",
			"SHA": "beecb3ff68cc233a0bb6c55a389cdd830e204917"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T23:06:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync submodules with diagnostics pipeline and service worker fix\n\nMulti-component synchronization enabling language extension diagnostics to render in the editor UI:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Extend DiagnosticsChanged event with per-URI marker payloads and cap keyring crate logging to Warn level. The new `changedURIs` field enables direct `IMarkerService.changeOne()` calls without extra IPC round-trips.\n\n2. **Output**: Add RewriteNodeModulesPath transform to fix hardcoded `vs/../../node_modules` paths that were causing grammar/tokenization to silently fail (returning SPA fallback). Also expose IMarkerService on `__CEL_SERVICES__.Markers` for SkyBridge to push diagnostics.\n\n3. **Sky**: Add `sky://diagnostics/changed` handler that translates Mountain events into editor markers. Receives `{ owner, changedURIs: [{ uri, markers }] }` and calls `Markers.changeOne()` for each entry - enabling red squiggles and Problems panel population.\n\n4. **Worker**: Remove obsolete precache paths from Service Worker that caused `Failed to fetch` errors on every install (paths moved to Astro chunks).\n\nImpact: Language extension compile errors, lint warnings, and type errors from extensions like rust-analyzer, TypeScript, and ESLint now render as visible markers in the editor.",
			"SHA": "7b62875b249ff5efc473887e164b325f25a135ff"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T21:54:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync submodules with Monaco worker fixes and polyfill telemetry\n\nMulti-component synchronization across the Land editor bringing stability improvements:\n\n1. Mountain: Fix 404s for extension webview assets by extending vscode-file URI handling to support arbitrary authorities beyond \"vscode-app\" in scheme.rs. Also reduce extension-scanner logging noise by capping ignore-related targets to Warn level.\n\n2. Output: Fix Monaco worker bootstrap crashes with InjectWorkerBootstrapShim (injects __name/__defProp shim into webWorkerServiceImpl.js blob factory) and RewriteNestedWorkerBootstrap (replaces .toString() pattern with JSON.stringified source). Switch RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef from hardcoded whitelist to auto-detection across vs/*.js files. Add __LAND_POLYFILL_TELEMETRY__ hook for monitoring.\n\n3. Sky: Wire polyfill telemetry through PostHog bridge to capture errors via PH.captureException with categorized properties (polyfill_category, polyfill_*).\n\n4. Wind: Remove deprecated Electron polyfill shims (ChildProcessPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, ProcessPolyfill, etc.) as functionality moves to Mountain's native Rust implementations.\n\nImpact: Extension webview assets now load correctly, Monaco language workers no longer crash on startup, production polyfill failures are now captured for debugging, and obsolete Electron shims are cleaned up.",
			"SHA": "ad74a242429d86ef0f9252befa6ac1e56c480063"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T20:48:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Output and Sky submodules with bundling fixes and initialization order\n\nSubmodule synchronization across three components:\n\n1. Output: Add HoistFunctionDeclarations and RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef transforms to fix TDZ errors in bundled VS Code after Rollup concatenation converts function declarations to expressions. Hoisting preserves unbundled semantics. RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef converts class self-references in static blocks from `ClassName.member` to `this.member`. Also updates InjectNameShim CSP and RewriteWorkbenchBaseURL for proper module graph tracking.\n\n2. Sky: Fix workbench initialization order by removing static pre-import of desktop.main.js that was breaking Electron service registration. The dynamic import in workbench.js now correctly sets up _VSCode_FILE_ROOT, NLS, and configuration before desktop.main.js module-initializers run, allowing native services (Disk FileSystemProvider, NativeHostService) to register properly. Also configures moduleSideEffects to preserve VS Code static initializers from tree-shaking.\n\n3. Cocoon: Bump protobufjs from 8.0.1 to 8.0.3.\n\nThese changes ensure the bundled workbench boots correctly under Tauri/WKWebView.",
			"SHA": "e7e25452f8c33f52f51ec74ada2b1779899239bd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T05:26:23Z",
